What users are allowed to do:
* forking it if it is intended to be a real OS. (they however, cannot name it Red-Bit,)
* using it as a kernel for operating systems.
* actually owning the software you flashed for your Micro:Bit V2.
* making videos on social media about the software.
* people are allowed to use the name as long as it is not a operating system.
* People can distribute their forks on other websites, however they first have to post them on GitHub, on the repo.
Anything else is not allowed by the protection of Copyright.
